# Line endings.
#
# Everything is stored in the repository with LF, and checked out with LF on
# every platform. Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default)
# rewrites files to CRLF on checkout — which breaks anything executed inside a
# Linux container, because /bin/sh treats the trailing carriage return as part
# of the command and fails with an unhelpful syntax error.
#
# The files that would actually break are called out individually below, but the
# blanket rule is what keeps CI, the images and a Windows working tree agreeing
# about file contents.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed inside containers.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# The lockfile is generated and enormous; diffing it line by line helps nobody.
pnpm-lock.yaml  -diff linguist-generated
